+MUTATION
+The loop claim's result was changed from:
+
+  str(palindromeFrom(S, I))
+
+to the deliberately false:
+
+  str(seqConcat(palindromeFrom(S, I), iCons(88, .IntSeq)))
+
+This appends the character code 88 ("X") to every claimed result. The source is
+preserved as spec-vacuity-audit.k.
+
+SATISFIABLE FALSE WITNESS
+S = .IntSeq (the empty string), I = 0, L = 1, J = 0, CALLER = 0,
+REST = .List, H = .Map, N = 0, with the claim's displayed scopes.
+Then 0 <= I <= isLen(S) and L > 0 hold. Actual palindromeFrom(S, I) is empty,
+while the mutation demands iCons(88, .IntSeq). Both trusted canonical Python
+and generated Python return "" for this input.
+
+COMMAND
+kprove spec-vacuity-audit.k --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY-AUDIT
+
+WORKDIR
+/tmp/audit-work/reconstruction
+
+KPROVE EXIT STATUS
+1
+
+HARNESS EXPECTED-FAILURE CHECK EXIT STATUS
+0
+
+BOUNDED RELEVANT OUTPUT
+kore-exec: Warning (WarnStuckClaimState):
+  The configuration's term unifies with the destination's term, but the
+  implication check between the conditions has failed.
+kore-exec: Warning (WarnUnexploredBranches):
+  1 branches were still unexplored when the action failed.
+Residual:
+  <k> str(S) ~> .K </k>
+  #Not (S #Equals seqConcat(S, iCons(88, .IntSeq)))
+  false #Equals I <Int isLen(S)
+  true #Equals 0 <=Int I
+  true #Equals I <=Int isLen(S)
+[Error] Prover: backend terminated because the configuration cannot be
+rewritten further.
+false_postcondition_kprove_exit=1
+
+INTERPRETATION
+The mutated file parsed and compiled, execution reached the result obligation,
+and the proof failed on the intended added-X mismatch. This is valid
